---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/guides/pricing';
const title = 'Shopify SMS pricing: compare the complete invoice';
const desc = 'Build comparable quotes, model seasonal usage and separate attributed revenue from incremental contribution.';
const candidates = ['postscript', 'sequenzy', 'attentive', 'smsbump', 'recart', 'omnisend', 'klaviyo', 'yotpo-email-sms', 'privy', 'firepush', 'sendlane', 'brevo', 'drip'];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/guides" class="link">← All SMS guides</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-xl text-cyan-100">A starting price cannot forecast a Shopify messaging program. Give each finalist the same destination mix, send volume and service requirements, then compare the complete invoice.</p>
    <article class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Make one quote worksheet</h2>
      <p>List ordinary and peak-month recipients, planned touches per flow, SMS segment counts, media use, email volume and expected profile growth. Separate currencies and destination countries. Ask for a dated quote with an expiry date; do not combine one vendor's promotional annual rate with another's monthly commitment.</p>
      <table><thead><tr><th>Cost line</th><th>Question to resolve in writing</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td>Platform and profiles</td><td>Which stored or active records count, which channels share a profile, and what happens at a tier boundary?</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Message usage</td><td>Are attempts, deliveries, segments or credits billed? How are failures, replies, SMS and MMS charged?</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Carrier and sender fees</td><td>Which destination, carrier, number and registration charges are included or separate?</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Implementation and service</td><td>What do migration, integrations, seats, reply coverage and managed services add?</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Commitment and exit</td><td>What are minimums, overages, unused-credit rules, cancellation notice and export costs?</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
      <h2>Price the final creative</h2>
      <p>Twilio documents segment-based SMS billing and explains that message length and encoding affect segment count. Its rules describe Twilio, not every app's credit system. Ask each finalist to price your actual rendered message, including personalization, links and non-English text. Request an SMS-only and a media version separately; do not assume a universal MMS multiplier.</p>
      <h2>A hypothetical contribution calculation</h2>
      <p>This illustration is not a vendor quote or a measured result. Assume 1,000 eligible customers split evenly into treatment and control. Treatment produces 30 fulfilled orders and control 20 at the same observation horizon. The illustrative difference is 10 orders; one small experiment alone would not establish a reliable causal estimate.</p>
      <p>Assume every order has a $120 pre-discount value and $54 variable product and fulfillment cost. Treatment receives $18 off every order, including orders that might have happened anyway. Treatment contribution is 30 × ($120 − $54 − $18) = $1,440. Control contribution is 20 × ($120 − $54) = $1,320. The difference is $120 before program costs. With hypothetical total message charges of $40, incremental platform cost of $50 and reply labor of $20, the remainder is $10. Apply discounts to all redeemed orders, not just the apparent extra ten.</p>
      <p>Reconcile returns and cancellations at the same horizon. Report incremental operating cost and the fully allocated recurring budget separately. Attributed sales alone do not establish profit; avoid assigning an invented dollar value to future opt-outs.</p>
      <h2>Compare models over the year</h2>
      <p>Usage billing follows activity, but concentrated peak sends can concentrate cash needs. Profile billing depends on the vendor's definition of a billable record; ask what happens when records are archived or suppressed. A contract may exchange flexibility for negotiated terms or services. Model each month with your own seasonal pattern and a lower-volume scenario that still owes any minimum commitment.</p>
      <h2>Keep the catalog useful without inventing winners</h2>
      <p>These are catalog entry points, not a ranking or a claim that each offers equivalent SMS functionality. Ask candidates to demonstrate your required Shopify event flow before comparing their quotes.</p>
      <ul>{candidates.map(slug => <li><a href={`/apps/${slug}`}>{slug}</a></li>)}</ul>
      <p>Sequenzy's pricing page currently describes email-volume pricing and an SMS/MMS beta add-on on paid plans. Evaluate its actual destination coverage, integration and add-on terms if considering it; a separate SMS provider is not automatically required. Keep an existing email tool when replacing it adds no useful capability.</p>
      <h2>Primary sources</h2>
      <p>Checked November 25, 2026: <a href="https://www.twilio.com/docs/glossary/what-sms-character-limit">Twilio message length and billing units</a>; <a href="https://www.sequenzy.com/pricing">Sequenzy pricing and beta scope</a>. No fixed vendor price or product winner is asserted here.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
